{#
  TOP BAND — Figma 911:547 (intro), 911:577 (status clock). With the rail (v4/rail.njk) all four share the comp's y=132 edge.

  THE INTRO IS THE PAGE'S 600px READING COLUMN (456px in at 1512, which is
  the comp). It scrolls with the page.

  THE CLOCK lives at the bottom of the left panel (index.njk, v4/status.njk).
  The right-hand track below only holds it on narrow screens, where there is
  no left panel: there it drops into the flow under the intro.

#}
<header class="v4-top">
  <div class="v4-intro">
    <div class="v4-intro__head">
      {#- 1155:10698: the logo follows the name, 4px on, centred on its line. -#}
      <h1 class="v4-intro__name">
        {{ site.name }}
        <img class="v4-intro__logo" src="/Assets/v4/icons/logo.svg" width="12.5" height="17.36" alt="" />
      </h1>
      <p class="v4-intro__bio">
        {{- home.intro.bio.before -}}
        <strong>{{ home.intro.bio.strong }}</strong>
        {{- home.intro.bio.after -}}
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="v4-intro__meta">
      <p class="v4-intro__location">
        <img src="/Assets/v4/icons/flag-nl.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" />
        {{ home.intro.location }}
      </p>
      <a class="v4-intro__email" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">
        {{ site.email }}
        <img src="/Assets/v4/icons/arrow-up-right.svg" width="12" height="12" alt="" />
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="v4-aside-track">
  {#- Empty on wide screens: the clock lives at the bottom of the left panel
      (index.njk). Below 1200 scripts/v4-clock-dock.js moves it in here, under
      the intro. -#}
  <div class="v4-aside" data-clock-home></div>
</div>
